# Evaluation quickstart

> Systematically measure AI quality. Compare approaches, catch regressions before deployment, and validate improvements with data instead of intuition.

[Evaluations](/docs/evaluate) let you systematically measure AI quality. Compare approaches, catch regressions before deployment, and validate improvements with data instead of intuition.

Each evaluation consists of three components:

* **Data** - A dataset of test cases with inputs and expected outputs
* **Task** - An AI function you want to test
* **Scores** - Scoring functions that measure output quality

 Set up your environment and [run evals](/docs/evaluate/run-in-code) with the Braintrust SDK.

 ## 1. Sign up

 If you don't have a Braintrust account, sign up for free at [braintrust.dev](https://www.braintrust.dev/signup).

 ## 2. Get API keys

 Create API keys for:

 * [Braintrust](https://www.braintrust.dev/app/settings?subroute=api-keys)
 * Your AI provider or framework ([OpenAI](https://platform.openai.com/api-keys), [Anthropic](https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys), [Gemini](https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey), [etc.](/docs/integrations))

 Set them as environment variables:

 ```bash theme={"theme":{"light":"github-light","dark":"github-dark-dimmed"}}
 export BRAINTRUST_API_KEY=" "
 export OPENAI_API_KEY=" " # or ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, GEMINI_API_KEY, etc.
 ```

 ## 3. Install SDKs

 Install the Braintrust SDK and required libraries:

 ```bash TypeScript theme={"theme":{"light":"github-light","dark":"github-dark-dimmed"}}
 # pnpm
 pnpm add braintrust openai autoevals ts-node
 # npm
 npm install braintrust openai autoevals ts-node

 # Install the bt CLI (macOS and Linux)
 curl -fsSL https://bt.dev/cli/install.sh | sh
 ```

 ```bash Python theme={"theme":{"light":"github-light","dark":"github-dark-dimmed"}}
 pip install braintrust openai autoevals

 # Install the bt CLI (macOS and Linux)
 curl -fsSL https://bt.dev/cli/install.sh | sh
 ```

 ```bash Go theme={"theme":{"light":"github-light","dark":"github-dark-dimmed"}}
 go get github.com/braintrustdata/braintrust-sdk-go
 go get github.com/braintrustdata/braintrust-sdk-go/trace/contrib/openai
 go get github.com/openai/openai-go
 ```

 ```bash Ruby theme={"theme":{"light":"github-light","dark":"github-dark-dimmed"}}
